    for f in ('A','B','C','current-derived','uniform','current-pack-quality-mass'):
        rows.append((f,num(comp['macro']['calibration'][f]),num(comp['macro']['development'][f]),num(weighted(f,'picked-quality-3','Brier')),pc(weighted(f,'build','top1InTop2'))))
    add('Offline lane metrics',table(['Model','Calibration next3 Brier','Development next3 Brier','Next3 picked-quality Brier (all)','Build top-color in top2 (all)'],rows)+'\n\nPrimary: same-pack next3 quality-card color-composition Brier, equally averaged over set, pack and early/mid/late stage. Secondary horizons1/3/5 evaluate future available cards and actual future quality picks separately. Targets normalize bounded quality/color mass; empty or unresolved/noncontiguous horizons decline. No prediction reads those labels. A current-pack quality-composition baseline tests persistence without lane inference.\n\nBuild alignment uses top-2 nonland spell-color loads from unique modal observed 40-card builds with >=3 games. Completed-pool labels require an actually complete terminal source inventory. Ties in predicted top color receive fractional credit. Calibration-by-pick reports prediction versus observed mass bins, not certainty of a binary open lane. [All metrics](docs/evidence/v2-phase-c/lane-metrics.json).')
    context=[]
    for f in ('complete-baseline','lane-current-derived','lane-A','lane-B','lane-C'):
        m=replay['Metrics'][f+' | overall'];context.append((f,m['Eligible'],pc(m['Top1']),pc(m['Top3']),num(m['MeanReciprocalRank']),num(m['MeanNormalizedRank'])))
    changes=replay['Changes'][best+'-vs-current-derived | overall']
    add('Contextual replay results',table(['Model','Comparable','Top1','Top3','MRR','Normalized rank'],context)+f'\n\n**{replay["Decisions"]:,} decisions / {replay["Drafts"]:,} drafts; {replay["Metrics"]["complete-baseline | overall"]["Eligible"]:,} complete comparable full-context decisions.** Partial pools, unresolved offers/labels, singleton ranks and unsupported pick15 do not enter comparative metrics. Their earlier valid observed cards remain explicit history; no truncated-pack ranking is counted.\n\nCandidate {best} versus current-derived L changes {changes["Changed"]:,} rankings, improves actual-pick rank in {changes["Improved"]:,}, regresses in {changes["Regressed"]:,}. It still loses neutral frozen L overall. Human selections are revealed preference, not truth. Q/A/D, weights, R/commitment, optimizer results and sparse priors are copied unchanged; only L and its recomposed score/rank/explanation change. Actual B.1 baseline aggregate metrics reproduce exactly.\n\nRuntime {replay["Seconds"]:.3f}s; {replay["Decisions"]/replay["Seconds"]:.2f} decisions/s; peak {replay["PeakWorkingSetBytes"]/1024**2:.2f} MiB. Engine/adapter/setup timings and optimizer calls are exported. Existing canonical importer/store and opt-in immutable evidence cache are reused. No second scoring engine or optimizer approximation. The reused CLI aggregate retains its legacy outer Q-report version; explicit Phase C L-only identity and format scope are in [execution scope](docs/evidence/v2-phase-c/execution-scope.json). [Replay](docs/evidence/v2-phase-c/contextual-replay.json).')
    add('Set-level results',table(['Set','A next3 Brier','B','C','Current-derived','A human Top1','Current human Top1'],[(s,*[num(comp['perSet'][s][f]) for f in ('A','B','C','current-derived')],pc(replay['Metrics']['lane-A | set='+s]['Top1']),pc(replay['Metrics']['lane-current-derived | set='+s]['Top1'])) for s in COMPATIBLE])+ '\n\nDMU multicolor/domain, BRO artifacts, WOE adventures/bonus sheet, LCI discovery, MKM investigate/List, OTJ bonus sheets/outlaws, ONE toxic/oil and MOM battles/bonus sheet are tested. ONE is a particularly large predictive regression. LCI slightly improves the primary metric, insufficient for the required 4/5 development-set gate. Derived feature availability is set-specific data; formulas have no authored archetype rules. Cold-start zero-data sets and Quick contextual behavior remain unvalidated. Build-color, pack/pick, commitment, lane-confidence and outcome strata are exported separately. Records never train the model.')
    early=[]
    for f in ('A','B','C','current-derived'):
        values=[lane['early'].get(s+'/'+f+'/0.5',{}) for s in COMPATIBLE];n=sum(v.get('earlyComplete',0) for v in values);locks=sum(v.get('lock',0) for v in values);false=sum(v.get('false',0) for v in values)
        early.append((f,n,locks,false,pc(false/n if n else None)))
    add('Early-lock analysis',table(['Model','P1P1–3 complete cases','Locks','False locks','False rate'],early)+'\n\nA lock requires confidence>=.5 and leader-runner support gap>=.5; false means the leader is outside eventual top-2 build colors. Sensitivities .25/.5/.75 are exported. Zero at this early threshold is largely **mechanical**: the ramp suppresses early support. It is not proof of universally accurate lane confidence. Eventual-build alignment and calibration curves by pick can grow later without forcing that pattern.')
    add('Recovery/switch analysis',table(['Model','Reversal episodes','Initially recognized','Recovered by11','Rate'],[(f,*[recovery(f)[key] for key in ('episodes','recognized','recovered')],pc(recovery(f)['rate'])) for f in ('A','B','C','current-derived')])+f'\n\nReversal labels compare quality-availability leaders at picks4–6 versus9–11 within the same pack, with a >=.05 leader margin and different colors. Recovery is conditional on recognizing the old leader at6, then switching to the new leader by11; mean latency is measured from9. These are post-scoring labels, not counterfactual table truth. Conditional denominators differ between models and may select different episodes. Development candidate/current rates are {pc(comp["recoveryDevelopment"]["candidate"])} / {pc(comp["recoveryDevelopment"]["current"])}.\n\nMean support L1 movement and non-tied leader-switch rates quantify stability versus responsiveness. Controlled reversal, aging, gold/colorless/land and boundary probes pass the intended invariants. The separate contested-blue counterexample fails the desired strong-closure behavior: A blue support {num(probes["candidates"]["A"]["blueAt8"])} -> {num(probes["candidates"]["A"]["blueAt14"])}. It is disclosed, not patched by post-development tuning.')
    u=next(x for x in gold['checks'] if x['name']=='Uldaros Theorix');uns=next(x for x in gold['checks'] if x['name']=='Unsummon');amph=next(x for x in gold['checks'] if x['name']=='Arcane Amphisbaena')
    add('Real/golden regressions',f'Production Uldaros Q={u["rawQ"]:.12f}, exact score={u["exact"]:.12f}; Unsummon Q={uns["rawQ"]:.12f}, C={uns["C"]:.12f}, R={uns["R"]:.12f}, exact={uns["exact"]:.12f}; Amphisbaena exact={amph["exact"]:.12f} remains ahead. Missing FRA positional data declines experimental substitution, retaining existing L—not overwriting its non-neutral live lane contribution. This fallback correction affects no qualified replay dataset or fitted parameters. Fixtures never select parameters.\n\n**Build passes, 0 warnings/errors. {val["CSharp"]["passed"]} C# tests pass, none failed/skipped; {val["python"]["phase-c"]} Phase C Python tests pass; {val["golden"]} golden regressions pass.** One existing WGC resource-bound assertion failed in an initial solution-wide run; isolated and final full-suite reruns passed, with no capture code changes. Exact cause is not established. Targeted tests protect indexing, confidence/surprise, aging/boundary/recovery, colorless/gold, no future leakage, held-out protection, complete component isolation, stream ordering and missing-data fallback. [Goldens](docs/evidence/v2-phase-c/golden-reference.json), [validation](docs/evidence/v2-phase-c/validation.json).')
    add('Development selection',f'**Frozen candidate {best}; development gate FAIL.** Primary objective is equally weighted next3 availability Brier across development sets/stages. Candidate A improves over uniform but is {-comp["relativeDevelopmentImprovement"]*100:.2f}% worse than the best reference, current-derived L. It beats all references in only {comp["setsBeatingAllReferences"]}/5 development sets. Contextual, early-lock and descriptive recovery gates pass; primary prediction and per-set gates fail. No human agreement or trophy-based retuning followed.\n\n**Why secondary gains do not rescue the position-only candidate:** predicting independent future quality-card availability is the preregistered target. Human agreement measures selected preferences, while recovery is conditional on different initially recognized episodes for each model. Neither establishes better openness prediction. A is only slightly better in LCI and loses in four other development sets, especially ONE. Its gains over current-derived L may reflect a weaker, smoothed lane influence that better imitates observed choices and transitions; that is an interpretation, not a measured causal mechanism. Its contextual Top1/MRR also remain below the frozen neutral-L baseline. Thus better secondary metrics cannot override the primary and per-set failures.\n\nA prospective integrity correction removed one incomplete calibration future horizon. The original calibration is preserved; the corrected pass selects **identical** family/half-life/retention/confidence/negative parameters, before development analysis. Qualified predictions and replay did not change. The zero-pooling versus positive-signal-confidence clarification was preregistered before temporal metrics. [Correction](docs/evidence/v2-phase-c/calibration-correction.json), [immutable selection](docs/evidence/v2-phase-c/selection.json).')
